diff --git a/README b/README
index 669ac7c32..3a5968c26 100644
--- a/README
+++ b/README
@@ -16,3 +16,90 @@ several of them using the Restructured Text markup notation.
 Please read the Documentation/process/changes.rst file, as it contains the
 requirements for building and running the kernel, and information about
 the problems which may result by upgrading your kernel.
+
+
+buildsteps arch64
+------------------
+ARCH=arm64 CRASS_COMPILE=linux-gnu- make defconfig
+
+ARCH=arm64 CRASS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- make j8
+ 
+Make file:
+
+~/qemu-10.1.0/buildroot-2025.08-rc3/configs/qemu_aarch64_full_defconfig
+
+
+with this content:
+
+# Architecture
+BR2_aarch64=y
+
+# Toolchain
+BR2_TOOLCHAIN_BUILDROOT_GLIBC=y
+
+# System
+BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_HOSTNAME="qemu-aarch64"
+BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ISSUE="Welcome to QEMU AARCH64 Buildroot"
+BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_PORT="ttyAMA0"
+BR2_ROOTFS_DEVICE_CREATION_DYNAMIC_EUDEV=y
+
+# Filesystem
+BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2=y
+BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_4=y
+BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_SIZE="512M"
+BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_GENERATE=y
+BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_TAR_GZIP=y
+
+# Busybox (all common utils)
+BR2_PACKAGE_BUSYBOX_SHOW_OTHERS=y
+
+# Networking
+BR2_PACKAGE_DHCP=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_DHCPCD=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_IPROUTE2=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_IPUTILS=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_NETCAT_OPENBSD=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_WGET=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_CURL=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_DROPBEAR=y   # SSH server
+
+# Debugging & monitoring
+BR2_PACKAGE_HTOP=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_STRACE=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_GDB=y
+
+# Text editors
+BR2_PACKAGE_NANO=y
+BR2_PACKAGE_VIM=y
+
+2. Apply and build
+cd ~/qemu-10.1.0/buildroot-2025.08-rc3
+
+make qemu_aarch64_full_defconfig
+make clean
+make -j$(nproc)
+
+3. After build, you’ll get:
+
+Kernel + rootfs at:
+output/images/rootfs.ext2
+output/images/Image (kernel)
+output/images/qemu_aarch64_full_defconfig
+
+A 512MB ext2 rootfs with:
+
+Busybox full set
+
+SSH server (dropbear)
+
+Networking (DHCP, curl, wget, iproute2, netcat, iputils)
+
+Debug tools (htop, strace, gdb)
+
+Editors (vim, nano)
+
+run qemu fron the path
+-----------------------
+~/qemu-10.1.0/buildroot-2025.08-rc3/output/images/start.sh
+
+qemu quit : better and safe use:poweroff (or )ctrl + A + C then quit
